/*
 * Declares the TemplateDefaultValue class.
 *
 * TemplateDefaultValue is an internal placeholder used during template
 * specialization. It represents a value that was explicitly provided by the
 * user(typically as a default argument in a template function or method), but
 * which cannot yet be semantically evaluated because template parameters are
 * not fully resolved.
 *
 * This placeholder allows the semantic engine to:
 *   - remember that a default value *was* specified,
 *   - defer its evaluation until template specialization is complete,
 *   - distinguish between “no value provided” and “value provided but not yet
 *     evaluable”.
 *
 * This distinction is essential for implicit calls, since parameters with
 * default values require a named expression to be considered “set”.
 *
 * TemplateDefaultValue is therefore a purely semantic artifact used to preserve
 * user intent during template resolution.

 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::literal::template_
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/literal/template_.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-03-05
